### Create: Rent (with category)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-02",
  "description": "Rent",
  "amount": -7500.00,
  "category": "HOUSING"
}

### Create: Salary
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-01",
  "description": "Salary",
  "amount": 25000.00,
  "category": "INCOME"
}

### Create: Checkers (no category, so it falls back to OTHER)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-03",
  "description": "Checkers groceries",
  "amount": -1250.50
}

### List all (newest first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions

### Get one
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/1

### Update: re-categorise Checkers as GROCERIES
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-03",
  "description": "Checkers groceries",
  "amount": -1250.50,
  "category": "GROCERIES"
}

### Delete: Salary
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/2

### Error: get a deleted transaction (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/2

### Error: missing description (expect 400 with field errors)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-05",
  "description": "",
  "amount": -50.00
}

### Error: zero amount (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-05",
  "description": "Mistake",
  "amount": 0
}

### Register: Thato
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Thato Khonkhe",
  "email": "thato@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Register: same email again (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Thato Again",
  "email": "THATO@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Register: second user with the SAME password (compare the hashes)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Lerato Mokoena",
  "email": "lerato@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Register: invalid input (expect 400 with three field errors)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 1. Transactions WITHOUT a token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions

### 2. Login with the WRONG password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "thato@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### 3. Login correctly (saves the token for the next requests)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "thato@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 4. Who am I? (uses the token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5. Transactions WITH the token (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6. A tampered token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi